# Recursion and execution-limit behavior regression cases (canonical)

# 1) Direct recursion should hit runtime execution guard (implementation policy)
# 実行時は ExecutionLimitExceeded 相当のエラーを期待
# A bare self-reference recurses; a vector literal does not (SPEC §4.3
# data-ization: `[ LOOP ]` is the data "LOOP", not a call).
# { LOOP } 'LOOP' DEF
# LOOP

# 2) Non-recursive custom word chain remains valid.
# Call STEP-A directly — a bare symbol inside `[ ... ]` is data, not a call.
{ [ 1 ] [ 2 ] + } 'STEP-A' DEF
{ STEP-A [ 3 ] + } 'STEP-B' DEF
STEP-B PRINT
# 期待: [ 6 ]

# 3) Guarded direct self-recursion in the tail of a COND clause. This is the
#    shape the internal backward jump ("internal GOTO") recognizes, so it runs
#    in O(1) native stack.
{
  { 0 LTE | 0 * }
  { IDLE  | 1 - COUNTDOWN }
  COND } 'COUNTDOWN' DEF
7 COUNTDOWN PRINT
# 期待: 0/1

# 4) Self-recursion reached through a NESTED code block. `{ FIBR }` is data
#    where it is written — MAP decides when to run it — so the call inside it is
#    an ordinary call, not a tail self-call. Keep this case executable: while it
#    was commented out, the trampoline mistook `{ FIBR } MAP` for a guarded tail
#    self-call and left the first element unmapped, so FIBR answered a wrong
#    number with no error and no NIL.
{
  { 2 LT | 1 * }
  { IDLE | [ 1 2 ] - { FIBR } MAP 0 { + } FOLD }
  COND } 'FIBR' DEF
[ 0 10 ] RANGE { FIBR } MAP PRINT
# 期待: [ 0/1 1/1 1/1 2/1 3/1 5/1 8/1 13/1 21/1 34/1 55/1 ]

# 5) The same shape through EXEC rather than MAP.
{
  { 0 LTE | 0 * }
  { IDLE  | 1 - { CNTX } EXEC 1 + }
  COND } 'CNTX' DEF
7 CNTX PRINT
# 期待: 7/1

# 6) A word may map a block AND tail-call itself on the same line; the direct
#    self-call still becomes a backward jump.
{
  { 0 LTE | 0 * }
  { IDLE  | [ 1 ] { 1 * } MAP [ 0 ] GET - MIXED }
  COND } 'MIXED' DEF
9 MIXED PRINT
# 期待: 0/1

# 7) Recursive design is explicit opt-in and testable
# 下記は意図的にコメントアウトした失敗ケース（手動検証用）
# { NXT } 'NXT' DEF
# NXT
